{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>בקהלם</b> — without a vav. <b>וברצנם</b> — even when they are in a state of favor." "<b>עקרו שור.</b> Targum Yerushalmi: וברעותהון זבינו יוסף דמתיל לתורא (in their counsel they sold Joseph, who is likened to an ox). Another interpretation: <b>עקרו שור</b> — the sense of חומה (wall), for the holem and the shurek interchange, and likewise the Targum renders: תרעו שור סנאה (they broke down the wall of Shechem). And it is the wall of Shechem."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:07.909997854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}